       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks like an error.\n\n**Metformin 4250 mg three times daily is 12,750 mg/day.** The usual maximum is 2,550 mg/day (about 2,000 mg/day for extended-release), so this is five times that. A single 4,250 mg dose is also far above the usual maximum single dose of 1,000 mg. Doses this high carry a serious risk of lactic acidosis, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the max standard dose)\n- **425 mg PO three times daily**, which isn't a standard tablet strength. You can make it with a half tablet of 850 mg.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO** at a different frequency\n\nTell me the dose you intended and I'll enter it right away. If 4,250 mg really is intended, please confirm that with your supervising resident or attending and pharmacy first. I'd also want a note on the order documenting that it was verified."
      }
